Falsifies `system_tests::user::elf_loader_tests::a_real_elf_from_the_initial_ramdisk_runs_at_el0_and_verifies_itself`.

Architecture: x86_64

The defect is a program entered without the stack its ABI promises: `image_self_checker` writes
its own `extern "C" fn _start` instead of `user_mode_runtime::program_entry!`. The kernel enters
with `rsp % 16 == 0`, the psABI expects 8, and `loaded_image_check`'s alignment check traps before
the program's syscall. aarch64 and riscv64 push nothing on a call, so the same edit is harmless
there and this record names x86_64 alone.

